    <section id="about" class="about" aria-labelledby="about-heading">
      <p class="section-title reveal">About</p>
      <h2 id="about-heading" class="about-heading reveal">Skeptics from around Greater Lowell</h2>
      <div class="about-grid">
        <div class="about-text reveal">
          <p class="about-statement">GLASS is the Greater Lowell Area Science-based Skeptics: curious people who value evidence,
            reason and the scientific method.</p>
          <p>We meet every month to talk through everything from pseudoscience and the paranormal to medical myths and
            the habits of clear thinking.</p>
          <p>Lifelong skeptic or just starting to question the world around you, you’re welcome here.</p>
        </div>
        <figure class="about-figure reveal">
          <img src="/images/region/middlesex-1856.jpg" width="1180" height="600" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
            alt="Hand-coloured 1856 map of the towns around Lowell, from Pepperell and Dunstable in the west to Dracut and Tewksbury in the east, with the Merrimack River winding through">
          <figcaption>Greater Lowell on Henry F. Walling’s 1856 map of Middlesex County.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>
